        "original_id": "4b77a34e-dd81-5133-9a9b-0d19fd69ac52",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Jacksonville station, Lakeland, New York City, Miami, Washington, D.C., Richmond, Raleigh, Columbia, Savannah, Orlando, Tampa\n- Products: Silver Meteor, Silver Star, Thruway Motorcoach\n- Companies: Amtrak\n- Systems: Silver Service, Northeast Corridor\n\nFacts:\n- Jacksonville station serves Amtrak's Silver Meteor and Silver Star trains.\n- Jacksonville station also serves the Thruway Motorcoach to Lakeland.\n- Amtrak operates the Silver Star as a 1,522-mile passenger train route in its Silver Service brand.\n- The Silver Star runs from New York City to Miami, Florida.\n- The Silver Star travels via the Northeast Corridor to Washington, D.C., then via Richmond, Raleigh, Columbia, Savannah, Jacksonville, Orlando, and Tampa.",
